counterfactuals.output:
A vibration damping device comprising:

- a tubular outer member;
- an inner member disposed inside the tubular outer member and spaced radially inward from the tubular outer member;
- a plurality of main rubber elastic portions elastically connecting the inner member and the tubular outer member, the main rubber elastic portions being arranged to define, together with the tubular outer member and the inner member, liquid chambers filled with an incompressible liquid; and
- a partition portion provided between adjacent liquid chambers, the partition portion including a restricted passage through which the adjacent liquid chambers communicate with each other,

wherein vibration input between the inner member and the tubular outer member causes elastic deformation of the main rubber elastic portions and liquid flow through the restricted passage, thereby damping vibration by a combination of rubber elasticity and flow resistance of the liquid.
